  "_comment_consecration": "Consecration is to a ritual implement what quality is to a weapon: the scale of how well-made and well-blessed it is. It is the ONLY thing that should move an implement's price. A gold dorje must not cost more than a copper one — they serve different elements, not different tiers.",
  "garb_fabric_ladder": {
	"1": "cloth",
	"2": "cotton",
	"3": "cotton",
	"4": "silk",
	"5": "silk"
  },
  "_comment_garb_fabric": "Ritual garb runs the consecration ladder like every other graded line, and the fabric marks where on it you are: unmarked cloth at the first grade, cotton through the middle, silk at the top two. It is a flavoured shorthand for the grade rather than a second axis — a player can read the rank off the cloth without being told. Metal threading was considered as an elemental axis and dropped: it would have multiplied the line without adding a decision."
}
